    "text1":  [
                  "Another fantastic Kennet Brothers' route combining the Te Awa river trail with the wild remote West Coast. Nothing too technical on this ride but you will need to be mindful of resupply spots in some of the more remote areas.<br>This substantial Waikato loop combines the smooth Te Awa River Ride with quiet rural roads, remote west-coast gravel and visits to the harbourside towns of Raglan and Kāwhia.<br> The riding is not especially technical, but don’t underestimate the distance or cumulative climbing. Long stretches between towns, exposed coastal weather and occasionally rough gravel make good preparation and reliable navigation important."

              ],
    "text2":  "At 345 km, the loop works best as a four-to-six-day journey. Strong riders can complete it in a long weekend, while a slower itinerary leaves time for Raglan, Kāwhia and the smaller communities along the way.<br>The loop can be joined anywhere. Services are considerably more limited on the western side, so plan food and water before leaving the larger towns.",
    "text3":  "Hamilton and Cambridge provide the broadest range of transport, accommodation and resupply. The route also passes through our home base in Raglan—drop into Cyclery Raglan for local advice, supplies or a quick bike check."
,
